// - During free phase, when model emits "<<", DON'T enter constrained mode immediately.
//   Instead, wait to see what token follows. The model will emit variable-content.
// - Only enter constrained mode for the FINAL << >> span at the end.
// - Approach: Let model generate freely until near end of budget (reserve ~150 steps).
//   Then FORCE open ONE constrained span with OpenConstrainedSpan.
//   Drive constrained content, close on completion, then let model continue freely.
// - But previous attempt (13) with this approach got 49% syntax - still bad.
//
// NEW INSIGHT: The evaluator says "balanced spans: 2/49" but "complete visible spans: 49/49"
// This means spans complete but not balanced = the ">>" is present but not matching a "<<".
// Wait, that's contradictory with "unterminated: 47/49".
